.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt WSET 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wset
.Nd change keyboard auto-repeat on Wayland
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Ar option ...
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes keyboard auto-repeat with the same options as
.Xr xset 1 .
Wayland has no protocol for this, so
.Nm
uses the desktop's own settings: GSettings on GNOME, which keeps them across
restarts, and
.Xr swaymsg 1
on Sway, which forgets them when it restarts.
.Pp
.Nm
changes nothing by itself, only the values it is given.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Print debugging messages to stderr.
.It Ic r Op Ic on
Turn auto-repeat on.
.It Ic r off , Fl r
Turn auto-repeat off.
.It Ic r rate Ar delay Op Ar rate
Wait
.Ar delay
milliseconds (1 to 10000) before a held key starts repeating, then repeat it
.Ar rate
times per second (1 to 255), and turn auto-repeat on.
Without a
.Ar rate ,
the rate stays as it is.
.It Ic q , Fl q
Show the current settings, as the compositor reports them to applications.
This works on any compositor.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Show a summary of the options.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Show the version.
.El
.Pp
Options are carried out in order, so
.Ql wset r rate 210 30 q
shows the new settings.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Wait 210 ms, then repeat 30 times a second:
.Pp
.Dl $ wset r rate 210 30
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xset 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Unlike
.Xr xset 1 ,
.Ic r rate
fills in no values that are left out,
.Fl d
does not take a display, and auto-repeat cannot be set for single keys.
